## 3. What you own, and what leaves your property

Your cameras record to a computer that sits in your house. Nobody else can watch them. Not us, not a
monitoring company, not a manufacturer.

You control everything from your phone, from anywhere in the world, over an encrypted private tunnel.
No ports are opened on your router and no video passes through anyone else's server.

There is no monthly fee you are forced to pay. If you stop paying us, the system keeps working
exactly as it did the day before.

If the controller fails, the lights still work from the wall switch. Automation is added on top of a
functioning house, not in place of one.

We cannot get into your system without you turning on a switch that lets us in, and that switch turns
itself off after {{ soporte.duracion_horas }} hours.

### The one honest footnote: mobile notifications

{% if notificaciones.modo == 'push_mitigado' -%}
You have chosen **push notifications with minimal content.**

Push notifications on Android and on iOS are delivered through the operating system vendor's push
infrastructure. This is an architectural property of mobile platforms. No application, from any
vendor, can avoid it without your phone maintaining a permanent foreground connection — impractical
on iOS and costly to battery life on Android.

Every competitor relies on the same infrastructure. We are telling you because you should know.

What we do about it:

1. The notification content is reduced to a **category and a time**. No image, no camera name, no
   location detail. What passes through the push service is the equivalent of "motion detected".
2. The image or clip is fetched **only when you open the app**, and then it travels over the
   encrypted tunnel from your own server.
3. If you would rather have no third party involved at all, you can switch to local-only alerting at
   any time. Ask us and we will change it.
{%- else -%}
You have chosen **local-only alerting.** No third-party push service is involved.

Alerts are delivered by audible and visual notification inside the property, and through a
self-hosted channel that your phone can reach when it is on your home network or on the tunnel.

The trade-off, stated plainly: you will not receive an instant notification on your phone when you
are away and not connected to the tunnel. You chose this deliberately, and you can change it at any
time.
{%- endif %}

